  "result": "Done — the gate returned **OK** on the first run (1 of 6 runs used).\n\n**What I wrote**\n\n`library/TrafficSpec/Concepts/motion/u_turn.lean` — the body, over the formals and the record's three claimed names only:\n\n```\nreversed ∧ uponWay\n  reversed := |headingSince u heading_step (|kin_yaw_rate u| > onset_yaw_rate)| ≥ reversal_angle\n  uponWay  := ∃ region w of kind highway. rel_occupies u w\n```\n\nThe onset is the definite rise of the standing condition `|kin_yaw_rate u| > onset_yaw_rate`; the accumulation is the formula language's `headingSince` with the declared time formal as its step bound, read through `.abs` so a reversal to either hand counts; the way is the one the body is on, with `w` anchored to `u` through `rel_occupies`. Two narrowings declared: the count anchors to the *latest* onset (the contract's own \"or a later onset starts it again\"), and the overlap is read at the observation the concept speaks about rather than across the whole manoeuvre.\n\n`library/TrafficSpecWitness/Concepts/motion/u_turn.lean` — one instance (heading step 2 s, onset yaw rate 4 deg/s, reversal angle 150 deg) and three built scenarios: `holds` (170 deg accumulated from a single onset, windowed to 7–9 s) → compliant; `fails` (a 90 deg turn into a side street, windowed to 1–6 s) → violated; `blind` (already mid-turn at the first observation, `kin.yaw_rate` absent) → unknown.\n\n**One thing flagged in `task_result.md`:** the `holds` narrative's halt. Under `headingSince`, an observed drop of the yaw-rate magnitude back to the onset rate followed by a rise *is* a later onset and restarts the count, so I built the pause as a 2 km/h creep and a rearward metre with the wheel reversed — the rotation continues counter-clockwise and the count survives from the single onset. A witness whose count survives an observed dead stop is not writable over this operator; that would need a different element in the record.",
